PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The deliberation remains divided between heat diffusion/propagation and Brownian motion, but historical and textual evidence firmly supports heat diffusion. In his 1900 thesis, Louis Bachelier explicitly equated the distribution of probabilities to the heating of a body under Fourier's heat equation, naming his discovery the "radiation of probability" (*rayonnement de la probabilité*). Because Bachelier was unaware of physical Brownian motion and did not name his discovery after it, heat diffusion/thermal radiation (or conduction/propagation of heat) remains the historically accurate physical process identified by Bachelier.
}

